 Daily fluxes (with errors and seconds of coverage) for protons and helium nuclei from the Ulysses COSPIN HET

 All fluxes and errors are in units of (s cm^2 sr MeV/n)^-1.
 Errors are derived from counting statistics only.
 The coverage given for each day is the total seconds of coverage in all valid H1-H9 counting rate 
 accumulations starting in the day, as listed in the HET Full Resolution Data Set Omni1.
 The Omni1 data set is available under Full Resolution Data in the HET section of the UDS. 

 As a result of the incommensurability of the readout cycle with day boundaries, the coverage
 occasionally slightly exceeds 86400 seconds.  The maximum excess coverage found is less
  than 30 seconds.

 Column  1 =  Fractional year - 1900                                                                               
 Column  2 =  day of year                                                                                          
 Column  3 =  H4 proton flux (39-70 MeV)                                                                           
 Column  4 =  Error for H4 protons                                                                                 
 Column  5 =  H5 proton flux (71-94 MeV)                                                                           
 Column  6 =  Error for H5 protons                                                                                 
 Column  7 =  H4 helium flux (39-71 MeV/n)                                                                         
 Column  8 =  Error for H4 helium                                                                                  
 Column  9 =  H5 helium flux (72-95 MeV/n)                                                                         
 Column 10 =  Error on H5 helium                                                                                   
 Column 11 =  Seconds of coverage during the day                                                                   
                                                                                                                   
